<title>USA: Vermont lawmakers scrap draft property tax bill.</title>
<headline>Vermont lawmakers scrap draft property tax bill.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vermont's House Ways and Means Committee has scrapped a working draft property tax relief bill, and cancelled a public hearing planned for this week.</p>
<p>The move comes in response to a Vermont Supreme Court ruling last week that the State's reliance on local property taxpayers to fund education was unconstitutional.</p>
<p>Lawmakers are concerned that current plans to ease the burden on property taxpayers may not be enough to ensure that all students have equal educational opportunities.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
